2026-09-27T10:25:12.2347658Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2347965Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2348373Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2348765Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2348906Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2349223Z ================
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2349429Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2349645Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2350162Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2351209Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2351384Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2351814Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2352085Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2352284Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2352828Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2353361Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2354342Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2355155Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2355313Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2355931Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2356710Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2357120Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2357583Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2358121Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2358402Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2358659Z ========
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2358816Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2360891Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2362941Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2363286Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2364040Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2365257Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2366180Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2367034Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2440277Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2441356Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2441516Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2441893Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2442117Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2443250Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2444356Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2445018Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2445900Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:25:12.2446112Z 
